#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110351 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/id #uuid "30974188-c734-5e99-a9ae-81d1a53b9105" :question/math-academy-id "e-14854" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched below.\n\n![](images/e5/e5393f15ff154f1f4cc310791790db0fe0ad0d9faa076d10f3f6ec7b481de086.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-3+2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110352 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/id #uuid "00575d99-28e6-59b7-b416-765808916fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14857" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x-1)(x-5).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=-(x-1)(x-5),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=1$ and $x_2=5.$\n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2} = \\dfrac{1+5}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110353 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/id #uuid "405e0230-69cb-5679-bec0-13a69c722934" :question/math-academy-id "e-14860" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2)$ is $x=6.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6,$ we will set our result equal to $6.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=k$ and $x_2=-2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k-2}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k-2}{2} & =6 \\\\ k-2 & =12 \\\\ k & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110373 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/id #uuid "04877936-271e-5fcb-a1ea-aa39c52482b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-19740" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $4$ | $12$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $9$ | $25$ | $9$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y = f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=4$ and $x=20$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(4) = f(20) = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=4$ and $x=20.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabolas vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{4+20}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e9f3df9-da61-5f4a-b3ab-8a1a1cda444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540607} {:answer/id #uuid "62de6123-6a95-5dae-88e9-843c5a0c968d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540695} {:answer/id #uuid "cac0d315-ce7f-5d80-9e6a-46b1ae01e841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540866} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0cfaa1-d45c-5039-a04f-63b0fdededc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540902} {:answer/id #uuid "e784cab5-862c-5407-ae59-9868332a3944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e9f3df9-da61-5f4a-b3ab-8a1a1cda444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540607} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba3ac59-9466-58f5-9b5b-efe7c90f5528" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "094a6192-1567-5375-9e5c-b0ab7210d2c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-106137" :question/problem "![](images/e1/e1fdcc8a8ed9dd9936ade0b088a672eadea1ca9ae7b12de7ce1b1dead2c3014a.png)\n\nFind the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=-4$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{(-4)+2}{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47acc35f-5b61-5d14-8bcc-66ac1ea76bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47acc35f-5b61-5d14-8bcc-66ac1ea76bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540654} :answer-field/id #uuid "caf9ab22-db76-5d02-b2ce-c710382a7b35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f8c9da4-4b17-554e-b183-7584d639d444" :question/math-academy-id "q-223659" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b0ebd3a9a282fca4dc4302549c22efe674ada772eb00ed5e8aa0abbe275074b.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a parabola. The $x$-coordinates of $A$ and $B$ are $-\\frac{8}{3}$ and $\\frac{11}{5},$ respectively.  Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola.\n\nThe axis of symmetry is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We're given that the roots of the parabola are \n ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{11}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{11}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{40}{15}+\\frac{33}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{7}{30}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8241bb7f-109e-55f9-be72-8316a22c2b01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8241bb7f-109e-55f9-be72-8316a22c2b01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540751} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da18180-5a36-5125-8324-5c1b0c6c8774" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b506000a-3cca-5384-98ce-1df2cd5d8561" :question/math-academy-id "q-223671" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x+7)(2x-5)$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=-(x+7)(2x-5),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-7$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-7+\\frac{5}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{2}+\\frac{5}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{9}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{9}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e1b4578-4b0f-5dff-8326-16f7e58f56a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e1b4578-4b0f-5dff-8326-16f7e58f56a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540716} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9a70c7f-9ea3-5d5d-821e-91e51ecf66e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cce9f3f-dd06-554c-bd43-11f02acc9108" :question/math-academy-id "q-223687" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(3x+7)(2x-k)$ is $x=-\\frac{5}{12}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{5}{12},$ we will set our result equal to $-\\frac{5}{12}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(3x+7)(2x-k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{7}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{k}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{3}+\\frac{k}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{6}+\\frac{3k}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3k-14}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{5}{12}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3k-14}{12} & =-\\frac{5}{12} \\\\ 3k-14 & =-5 \\\\ 3k & =9 \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1053c1f5-d753-5d4f-9ed6-23685e190240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1053c1f5-d753-5d4f-9ed6-23685e190240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540557} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1265d9c-4abc-5c77-ab0f-534e48c095b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65741bd8-a817-5dbe-b425-cf51f2c41352" :question/math-academy-id "q-223688" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(2x+5)(2x+k)$ is $x=-\\frac{9}{4}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{9}{4},$ we will set our result equal to $-\\frac{9}{4}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(2x+5)(2x+k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{k}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{k}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{5+k}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5+k}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{9}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5+k}{4} & =-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 5+k & =9 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f76139-8842-5f35-b9ad-0c15135ffd28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540569} {:answer/id #uuid "c5df1532-58f6-563b-be59-6d00c4c805e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540858} {:answer/id #uuid "cc78e255-475f-5616-99f4-98aaca4b83e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540868} {:answer/id #uuid "dad67dc5-057e-5f8e-85b6-70b06ecc7c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540899} {:answer/id #uuid "e222922a-273a-5cd0-8575-d106bef3f640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc78e255-475f-5616-99f4-98aaca4b83e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540868} :answer-field/id #uuid "41ffaac3-97a2-553d-9dc8-0e075e369f32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fc55d0a-3a99-52a9-a6f3-6f933c42885c" :question/math-academy-id "q-24855" :question/problem "![](images/a8/a8b1d42dd086ff74623c24989fd993c2946857e1744988135c6cdb18d9985b7f.png)\n\nFind the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{(-2)+3}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f6803f-552b-5156-8e55-974ff7420778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540533} {:answer/id #uuid "9021c496-ac44-55c7-8663-3a91757d6bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540769} {:answer/id #uuid "962ed523-4733-592e-b803-53eb8cc91d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540778} {:answer/id #uuid "a2eaa4b0-92d4-5639-9707-9998e5dc82bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540800} {:answer/id #uuid "b49faf21-ada8-5826-855e-4c177c412bdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2eaa4b0-92d4-5639-9707-9998e5dc82bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540800} :answer-field/id #uuid "93603e77-7010-5a96-87c7-8028b120d8c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfbab0dc-48e0-5fe1-b79b-211af0a386b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-30456" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=(x-6)(x+3).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(x-6)(x+3),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=6$ and ${x}_{2}=-3.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+(-3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5fc8d9c-e7fa-5efa-90c8-3d5291bec1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5fc8d9c-e7fa-5efa-90c8-3d5291bec1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540831} :answer-field/id #uuid "8173af61-504f-51e6-827f-522fb24ab912" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27fc5b3b-5534-585e-84e3-7a7fff1acf0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-311953" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $0$ | $2$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $0$ | $0$ | $80$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=0\\,\\text{and}\\,x=2.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{0+2}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e30ba9a-32b2-58e5-8851-f26d83233a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e30ba9a-32b2-58e5-8851-f26d83233a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540739} :answer-field/id #uuid "95bc64fc-fb2d-51a1-a46d-5a131f211674" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "269ed7f0-271d-546c-901b-64ac9bc840b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-311957" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $0$ | $14$ | $21$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $0$ | $0$ | $-20$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. The parabola opens downward. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=0\\,\\text{and}\\,x=14.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{0+14}{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b79b736-b329-566b-84ac-371cad2d3936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540574} {:answer/id #uuid "9087f1ff-3d38-5918-b9d7-4e44b4ce85f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540770} {:answer/id #uuid "99faed74-37b1-5272-8443-c6661f8de266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540785} {:answer/id #uuid "d276353a-b094-5edd-b49c-9bae1e03a9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540884} {:answer/id #uuid "f013a429-97bb-57bb-97ef-0165023ca02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9087f1ff-3d38-5918-b9d7-4e44b4ce85f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540770} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5497823-9601-508c-ab4e-5a578803285a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "158e2594-5618-53de-811b-cce07b6dc3b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-84897" :question/problem "![](images/ee/eeedf268b501345408b8192573072cbe21e9568c54f2abeead3d9f707748706d.png)\n\nFind the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=11.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{1+11}{2}=\\frac{12}{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=6.$"}]}
